From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Alexis Cruz-Ayala <alexisdavidc@google.com>
Date: Wed, 21 Oct 2026 09:25:08 -0400
Subject: [SkScalerContext] Guard unfiltered glyph bounds

When a mask filter is set, SkScalerContext::getImage regenerates the unfiltered glyph via a second makeGlyph() call and aliases origGlyph.fImage if tmpGlyph.imageSize() <= origGlyph.imageSize(). Because SkGlyph::imageSize() returns 0 when isEmpty() or imageTooLarge() is true, a non-deterministic font backend that returns an oversized glyph on the second load passes the size check and aliases the small origGlyph buffer, leading to a heap buffer overflow during rasterization.

Check for empty or too-large unfiltered glyphs immediately after the second makeGlyph() call, and guard against non-overlapping bounds before copying the filtered mask.

Bug: b/574221485
Bug: b/574214125
Change-Id: I6966d3b6f95de924e1a4f0e962761283640d35bc
Reviewed-on: https://skia-review.googlesource.com/c/skia/+/1400236
Reviewed-by: Florin Malita <fmalita@google.com>
Reviewed-by: Julia Lavrova <jlavrova@google.com>
Commit-Queue: Alexis Cruz-Ayala <alexisdavidc@google.com>

